%
W: 1. Ho, brother Teague, dost hear the decree?
W: Lilliburlero bullen a la
W: That we shall have a new deputy
W: Lilliburlero bullen a la
W:
W: (Refrain:)
W: Lero Lero Lilliburlero
W: Lilliburlero bullen a la
W: Lero Lero Lero Lero
W: Lilliburlero bullen a la
W:
W: 2. Oh by my soul it is a Talbot
W: And he will cut every Englishman's throat
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 3. Though, by my soul, the English do prate
W: The law's on their side and the devil knows what
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 4. But if dispense do come from the Pope
W: We'll hang Magna Carta and themselves on a rope
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 5. And the good Talbot is now made a Lord
W: And with his brave lads he's coming aboard
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 6. Who all in France have taken a swear,
W: That they will have no Protestant heir
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 7. Now Tyrconnell is come ashore
W: And we shall have commissions galore
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 8. And everyone that won't go to Mass
W: He will be turned out to look like an ass
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 9. Now the heretics all go down
W: By Christ and St Patrick's the nation's our own
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 10. There was an old prophecy found in a bog
W: The country'd be ruled by an ass and a dog
W: (Refrain)
W:
W: 11. Now this prophecy is all come to pass
W: For Talbot's the dog and Tyrconnell's the ass
W: (Refrain)
%
